# {{PROJECT_NAME}} Coding Standards

For new/materially changed code, prefer the selected industry language baseline within
verified build/CI, compatibility, public-contract, security/privacy, and platform
constraints. Existing conventions provide compatibility evidence. Report conflicts;
never bypass enforcement or start unapproved migration or repository-wide reformatting.

## Core rules

- Favor readable, cohesive code with low coupling over clever brevity or layers.
- Maintain clear comments for intent, contracts, and pitfalls; avoid obvious narration.
- Consider callers, failures, and verification; build for current needs, not speculation.
- Choose the best fit for requirements and maintenance cost, within required compatibility;
  explain material tradeoffs. Novelty or habit alone is not justification.

